      "release": "⏳ 未リリース",
      "body": "Closes #11663\n\nAdds a `coverage.ignoreNode` option for the v8 provider, to exclude code from coverage based on its AST node. It's for code that isn't in the source file and so can't carry a `/* v8 ignore */` hint, like the cache branches `babel-plugin-react-compiler` adds to every component.\n\nAs discussed in the issue, Vitest's built-in filters run first, so the user's filter only gets nodes Vitest doesn't already ignore.\n\nTests are in `test/coverage-test/test/ignore-node.v8.test.ts`: one checks that matching statements and branches are excluded, the other that the filter never gets `__vite_ssr_import_*` nodes. Both fail without the change in the provider. There's also a type test in `configuration-options.test-d.ts`.",
